   "subject": "Re: [shinyapps-users] How deploy the r shiny project to company's own website with https certificate",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Leo,<br><br></div><div>Applications served on <a href=\"http://shinyapps.io\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://shinyapps.io&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792360031576000&amp;usg=AOvVaw07WocNkieCplO8NQQEma9_\">shinyapps.io</a> are always served over HTTPS, so you need to ensure that any content in your application including content used by Leaflet is also served over HTTPS.<br><br></div><div>Also note when using custom domains applications are served in an IFRAME, where the outside frame is NOT served on HTTPS but the application inside the frame is.<br><br></div><div>Because you are a pro customer, I suggest you open a case with RStudio Support who can help you dig into this more.<br><br></div><div>-Andy<br></div></div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
